<section class="scene-network article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="scene-network-heading">
  <header>
    <p>Overlapping practices, not one origin</p>
    <h2 id="scene-network-heading">How the work assembled</h2>
  </header>
  <div class="scene-network__grid">
    <article>
      <span>Rooms</span>
      <h3>Basements and theaters</h3>
      <p>Poetry, improvisation, acting, comedy, and folk performance trained people to read a room.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span>Events</span>
      <h3>Benefits and ballrooms</h3>
      <p>Promoters learned permits, sound, lights, tickets, hospitality, and how to keep a crowd moving.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span>Experiments</span>
      <h3>Acid Tests and happenings</h3>
      <p>Audiences became participants while bands, projectionists, poets, and organizers shared the floor.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span>Communities</span>
      <h3>Farms and buses</h3>
      <p>Shared living became portable logistics: food, beds, travel, performance, care, and the next stop.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="scene-network__result"><strong>What emerged:</strong> a loose network of people who could make gatherings happen before the gathering had a stable category.</p>
</section>

